      "content": "Accessing a Character"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A string is a sequence of characters, similar to how an array is a sequence of elements. In JavaScript, you can access the characters of a string using indexing."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Consider the following example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "let animal = \"Cat\";"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Each character has its own index, starting from 0, as:"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "JavaScript String Index",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Now, let's access the characters of the animal string."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "content": "1let animal = \"Cat\";\n2 \n3// Access first character\n4console.log(animal[0]);    // Output: C\n5 \n6// Access third character\n7console.log(animal[2]);    // Output: t"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here,"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "animal[0] accesses the first character (\"C\")",
        "animal[2] accesses the third character (\"t\")"
      ]
    },
    {
